C. Commission calculation
Do not simply calculate commission on all orders created by a waiter.

Commission should be calculated based on configurable policies.

For example:
Policy	Example
Percentage	5% of eligible net sales
Fixed amount	TZS 500 per eligible order
Item-based	TZS 300 per selected item
Tiered	3% up to TZS 1m, 5% above
Manual bonus	Manager-approved bonus

For example, John generates TZS 500,000 in eligible completed orders.

At 5%:
\[
500,000 \times 5\% = 25,000
\]

John earns TZS 25,000.

But the system must define whether commission is based on:
- Orders completed or served.
- Amount actually paid.
- Net sales after discounts.
- Whether taxes are excluded.
- Whether delivery charges are excluded.
- Whether refunded or cancelled orders are excluded.
My recommendation: Calculate commission on eligible net item sales from completed and sufficiently paid orders. Reverse or adjust commission when an order is refunded.

Commission statements should be generated by period, with manager approval before payment.
