15. Important database and business rules
There are several design decisions I would establish before implementation.
Area	Recommended rule
Order ownership	Every order belongs to one tenant and branch
Waiter attribution	Store referral waiter and serving waiter separately
Commission	Calculate from eligible completed sales
Payment	Payment status separate from order status
Stock	Record every stock movement
Recipe	Optional, but available for restaurants needing ingredient costing
Payroll	Separate salary, advance, commission and payment
Refunds	Reverse financial and stock effects appropriately
Menu	Dynamic categories and schedules
Branches	Separate branch inventory, cash registers and staff assignments
Historical data	Never delete completed financial transactions
Audit	Record who performed important actions and when

I would also introduce an immutable financial transaction history. If a cashier corrects a payment, the system should record a reversal and a replacement rather than silently overwriting the original transaction.

For offline operation, queue POS transactions locally with unique transaction IDs and synchronize them safely when connectivity returns. Do not assume every online ordering or payment operation can be completed offline.
